body:json {
  {
    "content": "title: React Ace: Level Up Your Skills!\ndescription: Unlock your React potential! React Ace is your ultimate guide to mastering React. Dive into challenging quizzes designed to test and expand your knowledge of core concepts, advanced techniques, and best practices. Track your progress, identify your weaknesses, and level up your React skills with each quiz. From component lifecycle to state management and beyond, React Ace offers a fun, engaging, and rewarding way to become a React pro. Are you ready to become a React Ace?\n\n---question---\ntype: mcq\nquestion: Which of the following is NOT a fundamental concept in React?\noptions:\n1. Components\n2. Props\n3. State\n4.  DOM manipulation [correct]\ntags: fundamentals, components, props, state, DOM\n\n---question---\ntype: true_false\nquestion: In React, the `setState` method is used to directly modify the state of a component.\ncorrect: false\ntags: state, setState, component\n\n---question---\ntype: written\nquestion: Explain the purpose of the `useEffect` hook in React.\ntags: hooks, useEffect, side effects\n\n---question---\ntype: multi_select\nquestion: Which of the following are valid ways to define a component in React?\noptions:\n1.  Functional Component [correct]\n2.  Class Component [correct]\n3.  HTML Element\n4.  JavaScript Object\ntags: components, functional components, class components\n\n---question---\ntype: mcq\nquestion: What is the purpose of the `key` prop when rendering a list of elements in React?\noptions:\n1. To uniquely identify each element in the list [correct]\n2. To style the elements in the list\n3. To specify the order of elements in the list\n4. To store data associated with the elements\ntags: lists, key, rendering\n\n---question---\ntype: true_false\nquestion:  Virtual DOM is a real DOM.\ncorrect: false\ntags: virtual dom, DOM\n\n---question---\ntype: written\nquestion: Describe the difference between `props` and `state` in React.\ntags: props, state, components\n\n---question---\ntype: multi_select\nquestion:  Which of the following are common lifecycle methods in a React class component?\noptions:\n1.  componentDidMount [correct]\n2.  render [correct]\n3.  useState\n4.  componentWillUnmount [correct]\ntags: lifecycle methods, class components, componentDidMount, render, componentWillUnmount\n"
  }
}
